course: dictionary
lesson: 14789
title: Published
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To publish something means to print it or put it out so people can read it. Published is the past form, so «The book was published in 2015» means it was printed and made available for readers in 2015.
explain: Something that is published can be read by the public. A published author is someone whose books have been printed for others to read.
explain: Look at the words around published to work out its meaning. «Her poem was published in the school magazine» tells you the poem was printed so everyone could read it. The clue is «in the school magazine».
fact: Published is the past form of publish.
fact: Published means printed or put out for people to read.
fact: «A published author» is someone whose books have been printed.
fact: Published results have been shared so that other scientists can check them.
fact: Once something is published online, it is hard to take back, so think before you post.
exercise: «The book was published in 2015.» What does published mean here? | It was lost and never found | * It was printed and made available for people to read | It was written in a foreign language | It was read aloud at a party
exercise: «Mia is a published author.» What is a published author? | Someone who has never written anything | * Someone whose books have been printed | Someone who draws the pictures in books | Someone who reads books in the library
exercise: Find the word that means put out for people to read: «The scientists published their results so others could check them.» | * published | check | scientists | results
test: «Her story was newly published last week.» What does newly published mean? | Written long ago and forgotten | * Recently printed and made available | Read out loud at school | Lost in the post
test: Which word is the past form of publish? | * published | publisher | publishes | publishing
exam: «Once a photo is published online, it is hard to take back.» Why is it hard to take back? | Because the photo is too heavy to move | Because the camera has been switched off | Because photos never leave the phone | * Because many people may already have been able to see it
